Let $\mathbb{C}(q)$ be the field of rational functions in the variable $q$. The Iwahori-Hecke algebra $H_{n}(q)$ is the unital associative algebra over $\mathbb{C}(q)$ generated by generators $T_{1}, T_{2},\ldots, T_{n-1}$ subject to the relations $$\begin{aligned}
\label{e:Hecke1}
T_{i}T_{j}&=T_{j}T_{i},  ~~~~\text{if}~ |i-j|>1,\\ \label{e:Hecke2}
T_{i}T_{i+1}T_{i}&=T_{i+1}T_{i}T_{i+1},\\ \label{e:Hecke3}
T_{i}^{2}&=(q-1)T_{i}+q.
\end{aligned}$$

